  "status_text": "One extra bit flip makes three lights fit into six gates. Lean checked both sides on four switches turned on in order. A six-gate circuit can match the three light patterns with three NOTs, and every circuit under the same gate cap falls short with at most two NOTs (L-meta-53148). The search has also gained a way to reuse circuit checks across ordered switch settings. Lean checked that skipping or repeating settings preserves every sampled wire at the same gate and NOT counts (L-lib-1340).",
